1
00:00:00,280 --> 00:00:03,506
The product and quotient laws of exponents. When powers

2
00:00:03,506 --> 00:00:06,120
with the same base are multiplied, the exponents are

3
00:00:06,120 --> 00:00:10,491
added. When they are divided, the exponents are subtracted.

4
00:00:11,150 --> 00:00:13,250
Suppose we want two to the power four, times

5
00:00:13,250 --> 00:00:17,450
two to the power three. We could expand both:

6
00:00:17,450 --> 00:00:18,910
four twos, and then three more twos. That is

7
00:00:18,910 --> 00:00:22,630
seven twos multiplied together, which is two to the

8
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:27,510
power seven. Expanding everything every time is slow. There

9
00:00:27,510 --> 00:00:28,821
must be a shortcut.

10
00:00:29,483 --> 00:00:32,988
Let us watch the factors instead. Two to the

11
00:00:32,988 --> 00:00:35,752
power four is four tiles, and two to the

12
00:00:35,752 --> 00:00:38,923
power three is three tiles. Multiply, and the two

13
00:00:38,923 --> 00:00:42,143
groups join into one chain of seven. So four

14
00:00:42,143 --> 00:00:46,143
plus three gives the new exponent, seven. For any

15
00:00:46,143 --> 00:00:49,270
base: a to the power m times a to

16
00:00:49,270 --> 00:00:52,034
the power n is a to the power m plus n.

17
00:00:52,720 --> 00:00:54,780
Does the same rule work when an exponent is

18
00:00:54,780 --> 00:00:58,420
negative? Look at three squared times three to the

19
00:00:58,420 --> 00:01:01,360
power minus four. The base is the same, so

20
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:04,905
add the exponents: two plus minus four. That is

21
00:01:04,905 --> 00:01:08,033
minus two, so the answer is three to the

22
00:01:08,033 --> 00:01:11,107
power minus two. And from the last lesson, that

23
00:01:11,107 --> 00:01:13,651
is one over three squared, or one ninth.

24
00:01:14,277 --> 00:01:17,374
Now division. Take a to the power seven over

25
00:01:17,374 --> 00:01:20,011
a to the power three: seven factors on top,

26
00:01:20,011 --> 00:01:23,543
three below. Every factor below can cancel one on

27
00:01:23,543 --> 00:01:27,133
top. Three pairs cancel, leaving four factors. So the

28
00:01:27,133 --> 00:01:30,309
exponent is seven minus three, which is four. In

29
00:01:30,309 --> 00:01:35,003
general, a to the power m over a to

30
00:01:35,003 --> 00:01:38,948
the power n is a to the power m minus n.

31
00:01:39,580 --> 00:01:42,867
Let us use the textbook's example: four to the

32
00:01:42,867 --> 00:01:46,580
power seven over four to the power four. The

33
00:01:46,580 --> 00:01:50,308
bases are the same. Subtract the exponents, top minus

34
00:01:50,308 --> 00:01:54,087
bottom: seven minus four. That is three, so the

35
00:01:54,087 --> 00:01:57,871
answer is four cubed. And four cubed is sixty four.

36
00:01:58,493 --> 00:02:01,888
What if the bottom exponent is bigger? Look at

37
00:02:01,888 --> 00:02:04,553
five squared over five to the power five. The

38
00:02:04,553 --> 00:02:06,893
base is the same, so subtract: two minus five.

39
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:09,881
That is minus three, so the answer is five

40
00:02:09,881 --> 00:02:13,133
to the power minus three. A negative exponent is

41
00:02:13,133 --> 00:02:17,388
a perfectly good answer: it is one over five

42
00:02:17,388 --> 00:02:20,644
cubed, which is one over one hundred and twenty five.

43
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:24,000
Now put the two laws side by side. For

44
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:27,672
a product, the factor groups join, so the exponents

45
00:02:27,672 --> 00:02:30,800
are added: a to the power m times a

46
00:02:30,800 --> 00:02:33,320
to the power n is a to the power

47
00:02:33,320 --> 00:02:38,040
m plus n. For a quotient, matching factors cancel,

48
00:02:38,040 --> 00:02:41,378
so the exponents are subtracted: a to the power

49
00:02:41,378 --> 00:02:44,103
m over a to the power n is a

50
00:02:44,103 --> 00:02:47,108
to the power m minus n. In both laws

51
00:02:47,108 --> 00:02:48,851
the base stays exactly the same.

52
00:02:49,597 --> 00:02:52,677
Here are three mistakes to avoid. First: x to

53
00:02:52,677 --> 00:02:55,857
the power minus three times x to the power

54
00:02:55,857 --> 00:02:58,727
minus two is x to the power minus five,

55
00:02:58,727 --> 00:03:02,877
not minus six. Second: two cubed times three to

56
00:03:02,877 --> 00:03:06,634
the fourth has different bases, so the exponents cannot

57
00:03:06,634 --> 00:03:10,077
be added. Third: a squared over a to the

58
00:03:10,077 --> 00:03:12,647
power five is a to the power minus three,

59
00:03:12,647 --> 00:03:16,428
not a cubed. Read the operation carefully.

60
00:03:16,963 --> 00:03:20,312
Your turn. Three questions. Simplify two to the power

61
00:03:20,312 --> 00:03:23,288
minus three times two to the power minus two.

62
00:03:23,288 --> 00:03:27,663
Simplify seven to the power minus two times seven

63
00:03:27,663 --> 00:03:31,243
to the power five. And simplify four to the

64
00:03:31,243 --> 00:03:33,954
power seven over four to the power four.

65
00:03:45,373 --> 00:03:48,060
For the first, the exponents add: minus three plus

66
00:03:48,060 --> 00:03:50,640
minus two is minus five, so two to the

67
00:03:50,640 --> 00:03:54,409
power minus five. For the second, minus two plus

68
00:03:54,409 --> 00:03:57,613
five is three, so seven cubed. And for the

69
00:03:57,613 --> 00:04:00,421
third, seven minus four is three, so four cubed,

70
00:04:00,421 --> 00:04:02,204
which is sixty four.

71
00:04:02,817 --> 00:04:04,757
One last look. When powers with the same base

72
00:04:04,757 --> 00:04:08,337
are multiplied, the factor groups join, so the exponents

73
00:04:08,337 --> 00:04:11,557
are added. When they are divided, matching factors cancel,

74
00:04:11,557 --> 00:04:14,191
so the exponents are subtracted. Keep the base, and

75
00:04:14,191 --> 00:04:21,113
remember: multiplication adds, division subtracts. Thank you for watching,

76
00:04:21,113 --> 00:04:23,448
and see you in the next lesson.
